👥 User Roles & Access
Patients (Default Users)
Registration: http://localhost/Xiteb-Assignment/medical-prescription-system/register.php

Can:

Upload medical prescriptions with images/files

Add delivery address and time preferences

View pharmacy quotations

Accept/reject quotations

Receive email notifications

Pharmacies
Registration: http://localhost/Xiteb-Assignment/medical-prescription-system/register.php

Note: User type must be changed to 'pharmacy' in database after registration

Can:

View all patient prescriptions

Create detailed quotations with drug lists

Send quotations to patients

Receive acceptance/rejection notifications

🔄 Complete Workflow
Patient Registration/Login

Access: http://localhost/Xiteb-Assignment/medical-prescription-system/register.php or login page

Upload prescription via patient dashboard

Pharmacy Login

Login with pharmacy credentials

View pending prescriptions in pharmacy dashboard

Create and send quotations

Patient Decision

Patient receives notification/email

Accepts/rejects quotation in their dashboard

Pharmacy gets status update

📧 Email System (File-Based Logging)
Current Implementation:
Instead of sending actual emails, the system writes email content to text files

All emails are saved in the emails/ directory

Each email is logged with timestamp and recipient information

Email Log Location:
text
prescription-system/emails/
├── patient_quotation_20241201_143022.txt
├── pharmacy_accepted_20241201_143125.txt
└── pharmacy_rejected_20241201_143130.txt
Email Structure Example:
text
To: patient@example.com
Subject: New Quotation Received
Date: 2024-12-01 14:30:22

Dear Patient,

You have received a new quotation from City Pharmacy for your prescription.
Total Amount: $45.50

Please log in to view details and accept/reject the quotation.

Thank you,
Prescription Management System
Potential Enhancement (PHPMailer):
This system currently uses file-based logging, but could be enhanced with PHPMailer for actual email delivery:

php
// Example of potential PHPMailer integration
$mail = new PHPMailer();
$mail->isSMTP();
$mail->Host = 'smtp.gmail.com';
$mail->SMTPAuth = true;
$mail->Username = 'your-email@gmail.com';
$mail->Password = 'your-app-password';
$mail->SMTPSecure = 'tls';
$mail->Port = 587;
